## Runtime Surface

{{ if and .ProtoConfig.Enabled .ProtoConfig.Server }}* **gRPC** on port `{{.APIConfig.GRPCPort}}` — health and reflection registered.
{{ end }}{{ if and .RESTConfig.Enabled .CoreConfig.Enabled }}* **REST** on port `{{.APIConfig.HTTPPort}}`, base path `{{.RESTConfig.BasePath}}`. Per entity:
  `GET`/`POST` on the collection and `GET`/`PATCH`/`DELETE` on `/{id}`. Listing defaults
  to {{.RESTConfig.DefaultPageSize}} items per page, capped at {{.RESTConfig.MaxPageSize}}.
* `GET /healthz` — liveness.
{{ if .RESTConfig.OpenAPI }}* `GET {{.RESTConfig.BasePath}}/openapi.yaml` — the OpenAPI spec (authoritative list of paths).
{{ end }}{{ if .RESTConfig.SwaggerUI }}* `GET {{.RESTConfig.BasePath}}/docs` — Swagger UI.
{{ end }}{{ else }}* **HTTP** on port `{{.APIConfig.HTTPPort}}`.
{{ end }}{{ if .HasJWTAuth }}* `POST /signin`, `POST /refresh`, `POST /validate` — JWT auth, served on the HTTP port
  and excluded from the auth middleware. Signin authenticates against the
  `{{.UserEntityIdentifier}}` entity.
{{ end }}{{ if .HasKeycloakAuth }}* Keycloak (OIDC): send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; the middleware validates it.
{{ end }}{{ if .StorageConfig.Enabled }}* `POST /upload` (multipart `file`) → `{url, key}` and `POST /sign` (`{key|url, expiry_seconds?}`) → `{url}`,
  served on the HTTP port. They return 503 until the `aws:` config block is set.
{{ end }}{{ if not .InfoConfig.Disabled }}* `GET /` — the info page describing this deployment.
{{ end }}
